# CRITICAL — CSP inline-script hashes are computed over the exact bytes the
# browser receives (worker.js / serve.cjs hardcode the sha256 list, and
# tools/verify-csp-hashes.cjs recomputes it). CRLF in a served HTML working
# copy changes the inline <script> bytes and silently blocks every inline
# script in production (see commit v30, which re-normalized project.html to
# LF for exactly this reason). core.autocrlf=true would rewrite HTML working
# copies to CRLF on checkout — force eol=lf so no checkout can reintroduce
# the break.
*.html text eol=lf
